# README updates → commit & push

Whenever `README.md` is changed (docs, credits, deploy notes, feature lists, etc.):

1. Commit the README change (and any co-edited rule/docs that belong with it) in the same turn.
2. Push to the tracked remote branch (`git push -u origin HEAD` or `git push origin <branch>` as appropriate).
3. Do not leave README-only work as local uncommitted changes, and do not wait for a separate “please commit/push” message for that README update.

Still follow normal git safety: no force-push to main/master, no secrets in commits, no amending unless amend rules allow it. If push needs explicit approval in a restricted mode, request it immediately with the exact push command rather than skipping the push.
